Subject: overlayfs-drop-dcache-op-check

Stop ovl_dentry_weird() from treating DCACHE_OP_HASH and
DCACHE_OP_COMPARE as weird. Casefolded directories, which Android's f2fs
/data uses, set both flags, and overlayfs then refuses the layer. The
kernel the phone runs carries this change; the exact mount that needed
it on this device is not re-derived here.

Upstream: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common commit 5c5f2fea42dd4cc5ae1002945d86e305c09d3262
License: GPL-2.0-only, matching fs/overlayfs/util.c

--- a/fs/overlayfs/util.c
+++ b/fs/overlayfs/util.c
@@ -201,9 +201,7 @@
 		return true;
 
 	return dentry->d_flags & (DCACHE_NEED_AUTOMOUNT |
-				  DCACHE_MANAGE_TRANSIT |
-				  DCACHE_OP_HASH |
-				  DCACHE_OP_COMPARE);
+				  DCACHE_MANAGE_TRANSIT);
 }
 
 enum ovl_path_type ovl_path_type(struct dentry *dentry)
